|name2 = Toji & Kensuke Cats
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Toji & Kensuke Cats''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Similarly to [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]], Shinji Cat is used as a short-range tank to deal quick and high wave damage.

Despite having lower health, speed and slightly lower DPS than Cats in the Cradle, Shinji Cat has a lower cost, faster attack rate and [[Wave Attack]]s in all forms rather than just in [[True Form]] without a hefty Catfruit investment, making him slightly better in some situations, especially early on or against [[:category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies. However, as KB effects can knock metals away from your short-ranged critical hitters, it isn't of any use for them once you start acquiring reliable counters since it has no hope of eliminating metals directly.

Shinji Cat excels in stages where he can get a clean hit off due to it featuring enemies with LDs or low attack frequencies. Enemies such as [[Dolphina]], and [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] are good examples of this. Enemies with Omni Strike are also vulnerable, as they tend to move closer than they should be, hence causing them to take damage from the wave attack.

Despite his ability, it is not actually useful against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies because the vast majority of them stagger very easily to his raw damage, although it can still be used to recover ground against the likes of [[Le'noir]]. For Metals, his lack of Critical Hits ironically improves its utility, and can greatly hinder  various metals, such as [[Metal Cyclone]] and [[Sir Metal Seal]].

